---
id: org.dxos.plugin.illustrator
name: IllustratorPlugin
version: 0.1.0
---

A headless diagramming host plugin for `DXOS` Composer. Owns the `Drawing` ECHO type and the
agent-facing drawing skill and operations; the scene model, the `.dx` DSL and its layout engines live
in `@dxos/diagram`, whose [SPEC.mdl](../../common/diagram/SPEC.mdl) covers the stack as a whole.
Canvas renderers (plugin-canvas, plugin-tldraw, plugin-excalidraw) contribute a `VariantProvider`
capability supplying their canvas schema, a builder that maps the scene DSL onto their records, and
surface components; plugin-illustrator resolves the variant at runtime and delegates.

## Extensions

The following extension dialects are used in this document.
Each extension is defined in the Appendix or resolved via its URI.

| Term        | URI                            |
|-------------|--------------------------------|
| `type`      | `org.dxos.mdl.type@1.0`        |
| `feat`      | `org.dxos.mdl.feat@1.0`        |
| `scenario`  | `org.dxos.mdl.scenario@1.0`    |
| `component` | `org.dxos.mdl.component@1.0`   |
| `op`        | `org.dxos.mdl.op@1.1`          |
| `test`      | `org.dxos.mdl.test@1.0`        |
| `decision`  | `org.dxos.mdl.decision@1.0`    |

## Types

```mdl
type Drawing
  desc: Named handle around a renderer-specific canvas object.
  fields:
    name?: string
    canvas: Ref<Canvas>
```

```mdl
type Canvas
  desc: >
    The renderer's records, opaque to ECHO. `schema` names the renderer format (e.g. `tldraw.com/2`)
    and is how a drawing is matched to the variant that renders it.
  fields:
    schema?: string
    content: Record<string, Any>
    styles?: Record<string, Any>
```

## Capabilities

```mdl
component VariantProvider
  desc: Contributed by renderer plugins; supplies the canvas type, a scene-DSL builder
        (read/apply), a create factory, and Article/Card surface components.
```

## Operations

```mdl
op create
  key: org.dxos.operation.illustrator.create
  desc: Creates a Drawing with an empty canvas for the requested (or default) variant.
```

```mdl
op convert
  key: org.dxos.operation.illustrator.convert
  desc: Moves a sketch onto another variant by replaying its scene onto a fresh canvas of that variant
        (e.g. a read-only SVG import into Excalidraw); the old canvas is removed. Fails on an unknown
        or identical variant.
```

```mdl
op read
  key: org.dxos.operation.illustrator.read
  desc: Returns the current scene of a drawing as world objects with object-local coordinates.
```

```mdl
op edit
  key: org.dxos.operation.illustrator.edit
  desc: Applies scene commands to a drawing via the variant's builder; returns the resulting scene.
```

```mdl
op draw
  key: org.dxos.operation.illustrator.draw
  desc: Applies a `.dx` document: semantic statements of any diagram kind (structure, sequence,
        data flow) are laid out by `@dxos/diagram`, scene statements pass through. Nothing is applied
        while the document has an error; the result carries the problems and the layout report.
```

```mdl
op score
  key: org.dxos.operation.illustrator.analyze
  desc: Grades the drawing as laid out on one 0–1 scale, per layout constraint and cost term, with
        the diagnostics behind them.
```

```mdl
op generate
  key: org.dxos.operation.illustrator.generate
  desc: DEPRECATED, superseded by `draw`. Replaces a drawing with a diagram compiled from mermaid
        source (flowchart or classDiagram); the dialect owns the layout, so no coordinates are
        supplied.
```

## Commands

`dx drawing` (contributed through `AppCapability.commands`; React-free, so it loads in the CLI):

| Command                         | Effect                                                                         |
|---------------------------------|--------------------------------------------------------------------------------|
| `render <file.dx> [-o] [--plain]` | Lays out a semantic-DSL file and writes a `.dx.svg` (or bare `.svg`); prints the layout report. |
| `import <file.dx.svg>`          | Adds the drawing a `.dx.svg` carries to a space under fresh ids.               |
| `list`                          | Lists the drawings in a space.                                                 |
| `export <id> [-o]`              | Writes an SVG-variant drawing, edits included, back out to a `.dx.svg`.        |

## Dialects

Higher-level diagram languages compile to scene commands (see `@dxos/diagram`, `packages/common/diagram/src/dialect.ts`); each
dialect owns its layout, so its output lands as ordinary world objects that stay editable by id. The
`.dx` DSL is the authoring language; the mermaid dialects below are deprecated and kept working.

```mdl
component MermaidFlowchart
  desc: DEPRECATED. Mermaid flowchart subset (nodes, subgraphs, directed edges) with a layered layout.
```

```mdl
component UmlClass
  desc: DEPRECATED. Mermaid classDiagram subset (class blocks with members, stereotypes, generics, and the
        standard relation arrows) with a layered layout — supertypes above subtypes. Each class
        compiles to a world object with title/attributes/methods compartments.
```

```mdl
component UmlGrid
  desc: Grid variant — equal-size cells on the document grid (GRID=32), barycenter column
        alignment, orthogonal Z-routed connectors.
```

```mdl
component UmlEngine
  desc: Engine-backed placement (dagre | ELK layered) over the grid cells and routing — proper
        crossing minimization and straightness; see docs/DESIGN.md.
```

## Variants

```mdl
component SvgVariant
  desc: SVG renderer variant owned by this plugin (peer of tldraw/excalidraw): the scene DSL is
        stored verbatim as canvas records (SvgHandler/SvgBuilder) and rendered read-only via
        SceneSvg.
```

## Skills

```mdl
component DrawingSkill
  desc: Drawing via the `.dx` DSL. It teaches the semantic statements of each diagram kind
        (structure, sequence, data flow) for anything that is a graph, and scene statements, where
        the agent chooses the coordinates, for everything else.
```

## QA

Executable tests. Each step carries a human instruction (`do`) and, where the step maps to an
invocable operation, an agent binding (`invoke`). Report failures by test and step number.

```mdl
test QA-1: Create, edit, and read back a drawing
  desc: |
    The scene-DSL round-trip through the SVG variant (owned by this plugin, so no renderer plugin
    dependency is needed).
  actors: agent
  covers: []
  status: unverified
  given:
    - an identity exists
    - space: a space is open
    - collection: a collection in that space, to create into
    - no drawing named "QA Sketch" exists — ABORT rather than deleting one this test did not create
  steps:
    - name: Create the drawing
      do: In the navtree, click + on a collection and choose Drawing (or ask the assistant to create one). Name it "QA Sketch".
      invoke: [op:create] { name: "QA Sketch", variant: "svg" }
      capture: created
      expect: a Drawing named "QA Sketch" exists with an empty SVG canvas
      assert: return !!$created.object
    - name: Place it in the collection
      do: (no separate gesture — the navtree create action places it for you)
      invoke: org.dxos.operation.space.addObject { object: $created.object, target: $given.collection }
      expect: "QA Sketch" appears as a row under the collection
    - name: Edit the scene
      do: Ask the assistant to draw a rectangle labeled "Start" at the origin.
      invoke: [op:edit] { drawing: $created.object, commands: [{ _tag: "upsert", id: "start", shape: { _tag: "rect", label: "Start", x: 0, y: 0, width: 120, height: 60 } }] }
      capture: edited
      expect: a rectangle labeled "Start" renders on the canvas
      assert: return $edited.upserted.includes('start')
    - name: Read the scene back
      do: (no separate gesture — the canvas already shows the result of the edit)
      invoke: [op:read] { drawing: $created.object }
      expect: the returned scene's world objects include the "start" shape with the coordinates just written
      assert: return $result.scene.objects?.some((o) => o.id === 'start')
  after:
    - name: Delete the drawing
      do: Right-click "QA Sketch" in the navtree and choose Delete.
      invoke: org.dxos.operation.space.removeObjects { objects: [$created.object], target: $given.collection }
      expect: the row leaves the navtree and its plank closes if it was open
```

```mdl
test QA-2: Generate a UML class diagram from mermaid source
  desc: The UML skill's path (the skill is plugin-uml's) — replace a drawing's contents with a class diagram compiled from mermaid source, with layout owned by the dialect.
  actors: agent
  covers: []
  status: unverified
  given:
    - an identity exists
    - space: a space is open
    - collection: a collection in that space, to create into
    - no drawing named "QA UML" exists — ABORT rather than deleting one this test did not create
  steps:
    - name: Create the drawing
      do: Ask the assistant to create a new drawing named "QA UML".
      invoke: [op:create] { name: "QA UML", variant: "svg" }
      capture: created
      expect: an empty Drawing named "QA UML" exists
      assert: return !!$created.object
    - name: Place it in the collection
      do: (no separate gesture)
      invoke: org.dxos.operation.space.addObject { object: $created.object, target: $given.collection }
      expect: "QA UML" appears as a row under the collection
    - name: Generate from a mermaid classDiagram
      do: |
        Ask the assistant to render this class diagram into "QA UML":
        classDiagram
          class Animal { +String name +makeSound() }
          class Dog
          Animal <|-- Dog
      invoke: |
        [op:generate] { drawing: $created.object, source: "classDiagram\n  class Animal { +String name +makeSound() }\n  class Dog\n  Animal <|-- Dog\n" }
      expect: two class boxes ("Animal", "Dog") render with a supertype-above-subtype layered layout and an inheritance arrow between them, replacing the drawing's prior contents
      assert: return $result.upserted.length >= 2
  after:
    - name: Delete the drawing
      do: Right-click "QA UML" in the navtree and choose Delete.
      invoke: org.dxos.operation.space.removeObjects { objects: [$created.object], target: $given.collection }
      expect: the row leaves the navtree and its plank closes if it was open
```

```mdl
test QA-3: Render a diagram from the terminal and import it into a space
  desc: |
    The `dx drawing` commands: a semantic-DSL file is laid out headlessly into a `.dx.svg`, re-laid out after an
    edit, and imported into a space as an editable drawing. Recorded as a terminal demo by
    `autocue/dx-drawing.mjs`.
  actors: human
  covers: []
  status: unverified
  given:
    - dx: the `dx` CLI runs from the checkout (`packages/devtools/cli/bin/dx`) with the illustrator plugin enabled
    - an identity exists on the profile `dx` uses, with a space
    - pipeline.dx: a `.dx` file in the working directory describing `dx drawing` itself: five boxes in two groups
  steps:
    - name: Show the diagram source
      do: Run `cat pipeline.dx`.
      expect: the DSL prints — nodes, groups and edges, with no coordinates
    - name: Render it
      do: Run `dx drawing render pipeline.dx`.
      expect: |
        the report prints nodes: 7 (the five boxes plus the two group frames), 0 crossings and the output path; `pipeline.dx.svg` is written and opens as
        an image with the two groups laid out and every edge routed
    - name: Edit and re-render
      do: Append the ECHO space, EDGE and Composer nodes with their edges to `pipeline.dx`, then run `dx drawing render pipeline.dx` again.
      expect: the layout re-flows; the report reads nodes: 10 (eight boxes, two frames) and still 0 crossings
    - name: Import it into the space
      do: Run `dx drawing import pipeline.dx.svg`.
      expect: a Drawing named "pipeline" is added to the space and its id prints
    - name: List the drawings
      do: Run `dx drawing list`.
      expect: '"pipeline" is listed with the id the import printed'
```

```mdl
test QA-4: Showcase clip
  desc: |
    The 10s showcase clip: Draw shapes on an SVG drawing. Recorded light at 60 fps with no ident, captions or
    count-in by `tools/autocue/showcase/overnight.mjs`; the clip is the `clip: illustrator` step.
  actors: human
  status: unverified        # driven by autocue/showcase.mjs
  given:
    - an identity exists
    - space: a space is open
    - plugin-illustrator enabled
  steps:
    - name: Create a drawing
      do: Create a Drawing with the svg variant.
      expect: an empty drawing opens
    - name: Draw shapes
      do: Pick shapes from the palette and drag them out.
      expect: each shape appears
```

## Changelog

```mdl
decision D-1: Mermaid support is deprecated.
  date: 2026-10-25
  by: user:dmaretskyi
  affects: [generate, MermaidFlowchart, UmlClass]
  source: https://claude.ai/code/session_01JCCokgAuSJrLXWRkjTSY3V
```

```mdl
decision D-2: `generate` is marked deprecated and keeps working; `draw` is its replacement. Fills in [D-1].
  date: 2026-10-25
  by: agent:claude-code
  for: user:dmaretskyi
  affects: [generate, draw]
  why: The UML skill still needs mermaid's classDiagram to show class members, which the DSL cannot yet.
```

```mdl
decision D-3: The spec names the types and operations as the code does: `Drawing` with a `Canvas` ref, the `VariantProvider` capability, and the `draw` and `score` operations.
  date: 2026-10-25
  by: agent:claude-code
  for: user:dmaretskyi
  affects: [Drawing, Canvas, VariantProvider, draw, score]
  why: The code renamed `Sketch` to `Drawing` and added `draw` and `score`; the spec had not followed.
```
